    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17190" root="رى" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِىٌّ</span></b> : see art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">روى</span> ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  It is also said in the K,
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رأى</span>, to be a pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَأْىٌ</span>: see this latter word.
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>Beauty of aspect;</i> (K; and M in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">روى</span>;) accord. to him who holds it to be without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>; said by AAF to mean <i>beauty as implying</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَمْعَةٌ</span> [and therefore belonging to art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">روى</span>]. (M
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">روى</span>. [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِئْىٌ</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رأى</span>.])

